Mitcad's patch to OCCT 8.0.1, under OCCT's licence:
SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-only WITH OCCT-exception-1.0

Fillets: a section of a rounding's walk whose two contacts lie within the
walk's 3d tolerance of each other (a section of no width) is not taken
for a twist of the contact lines (mitcad#2300).

The case: the rim between a loft's side and a cylinder pulled from its end
face, convex in some places and concave in others, the two faces tangent
at the points between, split there so that each piece is convex or
concave all along and its rounding vanishes in a point at both ends. A
convex piece rounded with 5: the walk runs from one vanishing end to the
other (1054 points, both ends on the arcs), its last section 3.9e-7 rad
wide, its contacts 2e-6 mm apart. At that section
BlendFunc_ConstRad::TwistOnS2 said the contact line on the second face
runs backwards: its tangent comes from a system that is almost singular
where the faces are tangent, and its sign there means nothing. The walk
took it for a twist of the whole piece (TwistOnS2), and the stripe's
repair of twisted pieces, which needs a piece of some width at both ends,
gave up ("adjustment by reprocessing the non-written points"): the
rounding failed. The contact lines do not fold (the fold ratio of patch
2141's trace is 0.008 at most, folding above 1).

- BRepBlend_Walking::TestArret: where the section's two contacts are
  within tolpoint3d of each other, neither contact's twist is taken.
  Elsewhere nothing changes.

The patch's test and its before/after proof:
third_party/vcpkg-ports/docs/opencascade-patch-tests.md, section 2300.
diff --git a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/BRepBlend/BRepBlend_Walking.cxx b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/BRepBlend/BRepBlend_Walking.cxx
--- a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/BRepBlend/BRepBlend_Walking.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/BRepBlend/BRepBlend_Walking.cxx
@@ -1205,6 +1205,15 @@ Blend_Status BRepBlend_Walking::TestArret(Blend_Function&    Function,

     // Ici seulement on peut statuer sur le twist
     // Car les rejet ont ete effectue (BUC60322)
+    // A section of no width (its contacts within the 3d tolerance of each
+    // other: the end of a rounding that vanishes where its faces come
+    // tangent) has no direction of its contact lines; the sign of their
+    // tangents there, out of an almost singular system, is no twist.
+    if (pt1.Distance(pt2) <= tolpoint3d)
+    {
+      loctwist1 = false;
+      loctwist2 = false;
+    }
     if (loctwist1)
     {
       twistflag1 = true;
